      "overnight_surprise": false
    },
    {
      "title": "Crude firm, gas gains",
      "body": "- WTI is at **$102.51** overnight, up 0.7% from Monday's $101.76 settle, with the Iran conflict and peace talks still driving it.\n- Natural gas is up 16.0% at $3.02, the one big mover on the board, and the news gives no reason for it.",
      "so_what": "Gas moved a lot and nothing in the news explains it.",
      "conviction_level": "low",
      "overnight_surprise": true
    },
    {
      "title": "Cattle firm, hogs lower",
      "body": "- Feeder cattle settled Monday at **$349.90**, up 0.5%, and live cattle edged up to $229.975.\n- Lean hogs for December settled at $64.675, down 1.4%.\n- Farmdoc says the partial reopening of Mexican cattle trade still carries uncertainty over New World screwworm.",
      "so_what": "Feeders are still near highs while hogs sit at the bottom of their year.",
      "conviction_level": "low",
